<title>PORTUGAL: Interbanco issues 8 bln esc 3-yr bond.</title>
<headline>Interbanco issues 8 bln esc 3-yr bond.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interbanco SA is launching a three-year 8.0 billion escudo bond, indexed to six-month Lisbor plus 40 basis points (bp), joint leaders Banco Essi and Banco Pinto &amp; Sotto Mayor said.  </p>
<p>ISSUER: Interbanco, SA</p>
<p>AMOUNT: 8.0 bln esc</p>
<p>NOMINAL VALUE: 10,000 escudos</p>
<p>TERM: 3 years</p>
<p>ISSUE PRICE: 100 percent</p>
<p>SUBSCRIPTION DATE: 15 July 1997</p>
<p>NOMINAL INTEREST RATE: 6-mth Lisbor plus 40 bp</p>
<p>PAYMENT OF INTEREST: At six-month intervals from liquidation date, on June 30 and December 30</p>
<p>REIMBURSEMENT: at par, at end of third year of loan</p>
<p>ADMISSION TO QUOTATION: Second Market of Lisbon Bourse</p>
<p>LEADERS: Banco Essi, BPSM</p>
<p>CO-LEADER: Banco Espirito Santo (BES)</p>
<p>PAYING AGENT: BES</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
